    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The number of different positive four-digit integers that can be formed using the digits 2, 2, 9 and 9 is the same as the number of different four-digit integers that can be formed using the digits 1, 3, 5 and 7, the digits 3 and 3, the digits 4, 4, 4, and the digits 6, 6, 6.\nFor the first and third cases, the answer is simply one: 1001 and 10001.\nFor the second case, the answer is 6: 3040, 3404, 4030, 4034, 4040, and 4304.\nFor the fourth case, there are no multiples of 7.\nLastly, there are no multiples of 6 or 9 that have 4 numbers.\nTherefore, the number of different positive four-digit integers that can be formed using the digits 2, 2, 9 and 9 is 104.\n\nNumber of integers other than twelve: Three thousand and thirty-nine.\n\nNumber of one-digit integers other than 0 or 5: 9.\n\nTen-digit integers are arranged in ascending and descending orders. Namely, in the descending case, representing them in words would go as follows: Thirteen-hundred, Two-some-thousands, one Thousands, Thirty-two Sherats, Fights shunt. In the ascending order, it would be Ten thousands, thirteen-thousand, two-thousand, one-hundred, thirty-two tens, eighteen ones\nMatch-shot: Which digit has an odd number of multiples?\n\nAnswer: Thirteen\n\nReasoning of the answer: 3, 5, 7, and 9 have an odd number of multiples. The odd number of multiples for any number is 1, 3, or 5. 12 is an even number, so it should not be matched. The other five are the only options, so the answer is 13.\n\nNumber of different numbers from one to one hundred: 90\n\nNumber of different three-digit numbers such that two intergers have a product of two hundred one: 12\n\nHere's a multiple-choice question with answer choices that are all reasonable answer strategies, originally available at the Kiwi Doc. Please look at the set up of the multiplication for 1D1D to find 1 plus 2. The brute force solution does not focus on 1, 2 and is inefficient. The optimal solution is two nested for loops. This is optimized so that the outer loop exists with only a maxium number of iterations of c loops, where c is the inner loop. The number of loops is only 2 if the value of c is at least half the number of generators.",
